{"title":"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Variables)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Variables)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Using_Area_of_Square)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Using Area of Square)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Hypatia Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9719173013354488819bfa68a5aa42a58efad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\text{ cm}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />. When its length is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and its width is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the area of the resulting rectangle is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d1e8ea41f8a088cce281218d75afefcc7de19e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" />. Determine the percentage by which the area decreased.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Variables.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Variables)\">Solution 1 (Variables)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Variables)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the square before it is formed into the resulting rectangle. The area of the square would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b59ba357a1b54473c0c4dbe8672bb404f04770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />. Since the length is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the length of the resulting rectangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/2/9425be8e833f93c1b0ec2a5183b5e32b4195bb9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />. Since the width is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the width of the resulting rectangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e79eaefb29b6f01bc4d50407b0f2f010309f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the area of the resulting rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd63c19fbc9fc333910af02d2095158efcaa597c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3s \\times 0.7s = 0.91s^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9bf45bf613054a43593d04f750bd3959466dd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^{2} - 0.91s^{2} = 0.09s^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />, so we have that the percentage decrease was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/a/54a724b41258064060283155adef2aa44abcd701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0.09s^{2}}{s^{2}} \\times 100\\% = \\boxed{9\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"179\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Area_of_Square.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Area_of_Square)\">Solution 2 (Using Area of Square)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Area of Square)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The side length of a square is the square root of its area. Thus, the side length of the square before it is modified is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e1a4dddc507fa7a8af2c25da93798aa8001f4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{100 \\text{ cm}^{2}} = 10 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Since the length is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the length of the resulting rectangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/8107b7f87a60374200ff9d033bf177b19ae790a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.3 \\times 10 \\text{ cm} = 13 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />. Since the width is decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e5939a7bdd847ec86582225cd653c240b4abce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, the width of the resulting rectangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3feb4f8ec346cd2c2b22f81501d7e190e3e20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\text{ cm} \\times 0.7 = 7 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>This means that the area of the resulting rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a72a4a3ee8e298f687afbbea55b00f6fc1cf707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\times 7 = 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff00f71f2a4392f0cfedda93d3f4f7a28e94a381.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 - 91 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />, so we have that the percentage decrease was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/d/69dc6f0600bb177494002b52a5d0f2cc802c73b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{100} \\times 100\\% = \\boxed{9\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018032313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 102/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 79/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3920/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.833      1 2025_CEMC_Hypatia_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    5.833      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36316:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018032313 and revision id 281334. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}